<speak>
<s>From <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="zʊhd">zuhd</phoneme> news, this is your briefing for <say-as interpret-as="date" format="dmy">25032026</say-as>.</s>
<break time="1s"/>
<prosody rate="95%">
<s>Iran has called Washington's fifteen-point ceasefire proposal "negotiating with yourselves" — while fifty thousand American troops mass across the region and a thousand more from the Eighty-Second Airborne are on the way.</s> <break time="600ms"/> <s>Pakistan's army chief spoke directly with Trump to offer Islamabad as a venue for talks, after five calls between Pakistan's and Iran's foreign ministers laid the groundwork.</s> <break time="600ms"/> <s>Tehran has signaled it'll demand <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="streɪt əv hɔrˈmuːz">Strait of Hormuz</phoneme> control, war compensation, and a no-attack guarantee — all conditions Washington has already rejected.</s>
</prosody>
<p>
<s>In politics.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>Trump lands in Beijing on March thirty-first for the first US-China summit since twenty-seventeen — and China's spent the war quietly stockpiling Iranian crude while staying publicly neutral.</s> <break time="600ms"/> <s>That dual position gives Xi leverage over both Washington and Tehran before a word is spoken.</s> <break time="600ms"/> <s>Trade tariffs are officially on the agenda, but it's the Iran ceasefire terms that'll shape every session.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Kuwait has absorbed four Iranian strikes since late February, each probing a different system — a passenger terminal, fuel tanks, radar arrays, then fuel tanks again.</s> <break time="600ms"/> <s>Air defences intercepted six drones on Tuesday, but commercial flights remain grounded and the airport sits exposed.</s> <break time="600ms"/> <s>The pattern suggests Tehran is mapping Kuwait's defences methodically, not simply lashing out.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Denmark held its first election since the Iran war began, and Frederiksen's Social Democrats dropped from fifty seats to thirty-eight.</s> <break time="600ms"/> <s>She'd campaigned on Trump's Greenland threats and European rearmament, but voters punished her from both flanks — the anti-immigration Danish People's Party tripled its share to nine percent.</s> <break time="600ms"/> <s>No bloc holds a majority, and coalition talks could reshape NATO's Nordic flank at precisely the moment alliance cohesion matters most.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Park Wang-yeol ran a methamphetamine empire from inside a Philippine prison while serving sixty years for murdering three South Koreans.</s> <break time="600ms"/> <s>President Lee secured his extradition from President Marcos after the forty-eight-year-old was caught dealing via Telegram from behind bars.</s> <break time="600ms"/> <s>He now faces South Korean drug charges before returning to complete his murder sentence.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>A US congressman introduced a resolution on March twentieth to formally designate Pakistan's nineteen seventy-one Operation Searchlight as genocide — a campaign that killed up to three million Bangladeshis.</s> <break time="600ms"/> <s>Islamabad has never acknowledged the killings in over half a century.</s> <break time="600ms"/> <s>Even the bill's introduction breaks decades of American legislative silence on one of the twentieth century's largest atrocities.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>India's foreign minister chose a closed-door briefing over a parliamentary debate on the Iran war, even as the house was in session.</s> <break time="600ms"/> <s>Opposition leader Kharge insisted parliament — not a conference room — is the proper venue when a regional conflict threatens India's energy supply through the Hormuz chokepoint.</s> <break time="600ms"/> <s>Delhi backed open strait access in public, but the substance of its diplomatic position remains behind closed doors.</s>
</p>
<p>
<s>On the economy.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>Seven hundred and six ATM deposits totalling eleven million rand have been traced to accounts linked to former Eskom chief Brian Molefe — and the deposits shifted geography each time he changed jobs.</s> <break time="600ms"/> <s>South Africa's Zondo Commission laid out this forensic trail years ago, mapping cash flows to Molefe's successive homes and offices.</s> <break time="600ms"/> <s>Molefe now serves as treasurer of the MK Party, and no prosecution has followed.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>The EU has shelved its planned twenty-twenty-seven ban on Russian oil after the Hormuz closure drove Brent crude to a hundred and twenty dollars a barrel.</s> <break time="600ms"/> <s>Cutting Russian supply on top of a Middle Eastern shipping crisis would've been economically suicidal for European refiners.</s> <break time="600ms"/> <s>Hungary and Slovakia, which kept Russian pipeline flows under existing sanctions exemptions, now hold the leverage to block future energy restrictions entirely.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Punjab has launched a three-billion-rupee annual programme covering all adult cardiac procedures across twenty-four hospitals in the province.</s> <break time="600ms"/> <s>Each surgery is funded up to one million rupees per patient — the first programme at this scale in Pakistan's history.</s> <break time="600ms"/> <s>Whether the budget can absorb the province's surgical backlog is the question no one in Lahore has answered yet.</s>
</p>
<p>
<s>In science.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>A machine-learning model called INSPIRE retroactively predicted seventy percent of approved cancer immunotherapy matches, trained entirely on real patient records before those drugs were even established.</s> <break time="600ms"/> <s>The system ranks cancer types by analysing treatment events in medical histories, potentially cutting years off the trial-and-error process of matching drugs to tumours.</s> <break time="600ms"/> <s>Validation on prospective patients will determine whether the model works in real time or only in hindsight.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Europe's grid regulator found that Spain's twenty-twenty-five blackout was entirely preventable.</s> <break time="600ms"/> <s>Policy had locked renewable plants at fixed reactive-power settings, stripping them of real-time voltage control when oscillations hit the Iberian grid.</s> <break time="600ms"/> <s>Six and a half gigawatts of rooftop solar still sit outside any compliance rules, which means the underlying vulnerability hasn't been fixed.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>A single rink camera can now count youth hockey collisions automatically — a deep-learning pipeline detected eighty-six percent of head-impact events in full Under-thirteen games.</s> <break time="600ms"/> <s>Manual video review that once took three hours per match now takes thirty minutes.</s> <break time="600ms"/> <s>Leagues can measure collision exposure without wearable sensors, turning concussion tracking from a research exercise into something any arena can deploy.</s>
</p>
<p>
<s>In technology.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>AI training clusters now exceed a hundred megawatts, and the energy lost at each AC-to-DC conversion stage is adding up fast.</s> <break time="600ms"/> <s>Data centres are reversing Edison's eighteen-eighties defeat by shifting from alternating to direct current distribution, cutting power waste by ten to twenty percent.</s> <break time="600ms"/> <s>Facilities that delay the switch face compounding energy costs as AI infrastructure scales — and it's scaling quickly.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Trade finance still runs on faxed letters of credit, and Ripple's betting its dollar-backed stablecoin can replace them.</s> <break time="600ms"/> <s>The company joined Singapore's central bank sandbox to test automatic payment release when shipments are verified, targeting a ten-trillion-dollar market built on days-long manual settlement.</s> <break time="600ms"/> <s>Full regulatory clearance is still required before a single real trade can settle this way, God willing.</s>
</p>
<break time="1s"/>
<prosody rate="90%">
<s>That's your briefing from <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="zʊhd">zuhd</phoneme> news.</s>
</prosody>
</speak>